  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 1.08,
      "end_seconds": 3.44,
      "duration_seconds": 2.36,
      "text": "Afternoon, thanks for coming in."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 5.4,
      "end_seconds": 9.36,
      "duration_seconds": 3.96,
      "text": "Oh, morning, doctor, sorry about the rush."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 10.65,
      "end_seconds": 13.49,
      "duration_seconds": 2.84,
      "text": "What do you need help with?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 14.52,
      "end_seconds": 19.04,
      "duration_seconds": 4.52,
      "text": "So, I've been feeling like I have flu, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 20.74,
      "end_seconds": 24.96,
      "duration_seconds": 4.22,
      "text": "Can I check a few measurements before we carry on?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 36.66,
      "end_seconds": 39.62,
      "duration_seconds": 2.96,
      "text": "Keep your arm relaxed for me..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 58.23,
      "end_seconds": 73.87,
      "duration_seconds": 15.64,
      "text": "Okay: respiratory rate 16, BMI works out to 26.6, temperature 36.6. And heart rate 120, height 184 centimetres, SpO2 97 percent on room air, blood pressure 134 over 74, weight 90 kilos."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 86.24,
      "end_seconds": 87.64,
      "duration_seconds": 1.4,
      "text": "Since when exactly?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 88.85,
      "end_seconds": 92.29,
      "duration_seconds": 3.44,
      "text": "It's been like this since last night."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 92.86,
      "end_seconds": 96.47,
      "duration_seconds": 3.61,
      "text": "Right, how strong would you say it is?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 97.57,
      "end_seconds": 99.01,
      "duration_seconds": 1.44,
      "text": "I'd say severe."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 100.54,
      "end_seconds": 103.75,
      "duration_seconds": 3.21,
      "text": "Right, is there anything else with it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 105.12,
      "end_seconds": 116.08,
      "duration_seconds": 10.96,
      "text": "When it starts I tend to get being very thirsty as well. The being very thirsty? That's been for six months."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 118.11,
      "end_seconds": 120.96,
      "duration_seconds": 2.85,
      "text": "How much does it limit you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 122.15,
      "end_seconds": 123.11,
      "duration_seconds": 0.96,
      "text": "Mostly moderate."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 138.85,
      "end_seconds": 142.26,
      "duration_seconds": 3.41,
      "text": "Any fever, sore throat or diarrhoea at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 142.88,
      "end_seconds": 149.09,
      "duration_seconds": 6.21,
      "text": "Let me think, I haven't had fever, sore throat or diarrhoea, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 151.19,
      "end_seconds": 152.51,
      "duration_seconds": 1.32,
      "text": "What about cough?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 154.48,
      "end_seconds": 157.64,
      "duration_seconds": 3.16,
      "text": "No, I haven't had any cough."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 158.69,
      "end_seconds": 160.5,
      "duration_seconds": 1.81,
      "text": "Right, neurologically, anything strange?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 162.24,
      "end_seconds": 164.2,
      "duration_seconds": 1.96,
      "text": "No, nothing like that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 165.91,
      "end_seconds": 169.35,
      "duration_seconds": 3.44,
      "text": "How are your joints, any aches elsewhere?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 174.88,
      "end_seconds": 176.51,
      "duration_seconds": 1.63,
      "text": "No, nothing there."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 177.73,
      "end_seconds": 182.46,
      "duration_seconds": 4.73,
      "text": "Any allergies to tablets, food or anything in the environment?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 183.37,
      "end_seconds": 186.82,
      "duration_seconds": 3.45,
      "text": "I mean, I've never had an allergy."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 191.75,
      "end_seconds": 196.01,
      "duration_seconds": 4.26,
      "text": "Do you have any medical conditions I should know about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 197.78,
      "end_seconds": 200.95,
      "duration_seconds": 3.17,
      "text": "No, nothing I can think of."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 202.84,
      "end_seconds": 206.4,
      "duration_seconds": 3.56,
      "text": "What does a normal day of food look like?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 207.1,
      "end_seconds": 210.9,
      "duration_seconds": 3.8,
      "text": "Lots of rice, lentils and some fruit."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 212.38,
      "end_seconds": 214.54,
      "duration_seconds": 2.16,
      "text": "Right, how active are you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 215.53,
      "end_seconds": 218.8,
      "duration_seconds": 3.27,
      "text": "I hardly move around during the day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 233.71,
      "end_seconds": 236.65,
      "duration_seconds": 2.94,
      "text": "So, are you on any regular medication?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 237.28,
      "end_seconds": 239.64,
      "duration_seconds": 2.36,
      "text": "No, nothing at the moment."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 242.53,
      "end_seconds": 246.87,
      "duration_seconds": 4.34,
      "text": "I'll examine you in a second, make yourself comfortable."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 248.72,
      "end_seconds": 250.72,
      "duration_seconds": 2.0,
      "text": "Tell me if that's sore."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 261.06,
      "end_seconds": 267.0,
      "duration_seconds": 5.94,
      "text": "You are breathing a little deeply and fast and your mouth is dry."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 271.82,
      "end_seconds": 287.93,
      "duration_seconds": 16.11,
      "text": "You can sit up now. Right, here's what I'm thinking. It's hard to say. Possible new type 1 diabetes starting to turn acidic is one possibility and a viral illness another, and I'd rather not commit yet."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 289.99,
      "end_seconds": 292.72,
      "duration_seconds": 2.73,
      "text": "Do you think it's something serious?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 293.75,
      "end_seconds": 316.46,
      "duration_seconds": 22.71,
      "text": "Nothing I've seen today points to an emergency. It looks like possible new type 1 diabetes starting to turn acidic, but I'd like to confirm. So, to recap quickly. You've been feeling like you have flu, since last night, severe, and no fever or cough."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 317.24,
      "end_seconds": 319.18,
      "duration_seconds": 1.94,
      "text": "That's what happened, yes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 320.6,
      "end_seconds": 346.16,
      "duration_seconds": 25.56,
      "text": "I think blood tests makes sense here, for possible ketoacidosis. The result will help us decide whether anything more is needed. Let's get a finger-prick glucose and ketones, for thirst and weight loss. This is not flu, your sugar is very high, and you need hospital insulin today. Please come and see me straight away. That's all from me. Any questions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 346.67,
      "end_seconds": 349.56,
      "duration_seconds": 2.89,
      "text": "I think I understand everything. Thanks."
    }
  ]
}